{"id":"yodel-muc","title":"Set up Bazel remote cache for CI/release","description":"Bazel rebuilds everything from scratch each release (~87s for analyze+build). A remote cache (e.g. BuildBuddy free tier or GCS bucket) would make incremental releases near-instant. Steps: 1) Choose provider (BuildBuddy recommended - free for open source). 2) Create account, get API key. 3) Add to .bazelrc: build --remote_cache=grpcs://remote.buildbuddy.io and build --remote_header=x-buildbuddy-api-key=$API_KEY. 4) Store API key as GitHub secret. 5) Add --remote_header flag in CI/release workflows via env var. Expected savings: ~40-80s per release, ~60-90s per CI run.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"stef@iamstef.net","created_at":"2026-02-14T21:48:50.316723-07:00","created_by":"Stefan Penner","updated_at":"2026-02-14T21:48:50.316723-07:00"}
