{"id":"yodel-yjg","title":"Explore async notarization to overlap with release steps","description":"Currently notarization blocks for ~48s with --wait. Could submit notarization, do GitHub release creation in parallel, then poll for completion and staple. Approach: 1) Submit DMG with 'xcrun notarytool submit' (no --wait), capture submission ID. 2) Create GitHub release with un-stapled DMG. 3) Poll notarytool for completion. 4) Staple ticket to DMG. 5) Update release asset with stapled DMG. Trade-off: adds complexity for ~30s savings. May not be worth it given other optimizations.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"stef@iamstef.net","created_at":"2026-02-14T21:48:51.151933-07:00","created_by":"Stefan Penner","updated_at":"2026-02-14T21:48:51.151933-07:00"}
